WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.080
How's my hair looking?

00:00:05.080 --> 00:00:09.940
In March, I said US-China trade was "all talk, no action." Now, it's "all yelling, no action."

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.880
The yelling stems from American tariffs on up to $450 billion dollars in Chinese imports. Tariffs are a mistake.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:22.020
They would hurt American consumers. They would hit Chinese companies which have done nothing wrong, along with the predatory companies.

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:27.200
China does heavily subsidize its firms while enjoying open competition practiced by others.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:33.100
It steals and coerces transfer of American intellectual property. It promises to improve, but it never does.

00:00:33.100 --> 00:00:39.460
We should respond to that, just not with tariffs. The US should target large enterprises owned by the Chinese government.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.060
The Communist Party wants these enterprises to dominate the Chinese and global economies.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:48.440
Because they are owned by the government, they can be held responsible for policy.

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.480
The US should start with a small group of bad offenders with regard to IP.

00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:58.880
They should not be allowed to do business with American consumers or companies. They should be hit with global financial sanctions.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:07.120
This maximizes the pressure on bad Chinese actors without taxing Americans. It's more focused and more justified than tariffs.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.100
What do you think about the US Responding to China with tariffs? Let us know in your comments.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.020
Also, let us know what other topics you'd like our scholars to cover in 60 seconds

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:20.020
and be sure to LIKE and subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

